# Nix environment (agent shell)

Node, npm, make, kubectl, and other tools come from the repo's Nix flake; there is no global Node.
Load the cached environment once per agent shell, from the repo root. The shell keeps it, so
later commands run tools directly:

```bash
eval "$(direnv export zsh)" && node --version
```

If `node` is still missing (stale direnv cache after a `flake.lock` change), prefix commands with
`./scripts/nix/with-env <command>`, which starts `nix develop` each call. Request full
permissions so Nix can write `~/.cache/nix`. Commands given to the operator stay plain; their
shell runs direnv.
